                            <comment id="17786682" author="JIRAUSER303052" created="Thu, 16 Nov 2023 09:12:52 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Initially localized to:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Individually, spring-boot-autoconfigure is downgraded to 2.6.14-2.7.11, spring-boot stays at 2.7.12, and starting KE initializes the cookieSerializer and then the AppInitializer&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &amp;lt;dependency&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &amp;lt;groupId&amp;gt;org.springframework.boot&amp;lt;/groupId&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &amp;lt;artifactId&amp;gt;spring-boot-autoconfigure&amp;lt;/artifactId&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &amp;lt;version&amp;gt;2.6.14&amp;lt;/version&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &amp;lt;/dependency&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Only spring-boot-autoconfigure 2.7.12 has a problem&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;RC%C2%A0&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;RC&#160;&lt;/h2&gt;


&lt;p&gt;2.7.12 entered a commit: Prevent early initialization of SessionRepository beans&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/issues/35240&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/issues/35240&lt;/a&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The dependencies in kylin cookieSerializer are as follows&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/13064453/13064453_image-2023-11-16-17-09-47-295.png&quot; height=&quot;588&quot; width=&quot;1068&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.session.SessionRepositoryFilterConfiguration.sessionRepositoryFilterRegistration(org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.session.SessionProperties,org.springframework.session.web.http.SessionRepositoryFilter&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#FF0000&quot;&gt;So the cookieSerializer is not initialized preferentially&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;FixDesign&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Fix Design&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;By injecting the cookieSerializer into the AppInitializer, the cookieSerializer will be initialized before the init, and the meta_url read will be the original value.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
